---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Biographical context, dualist editor philosophy, and open source contributions.">
	<article class="about-article">
		<header class="about-header">
			<h1>About me</h1>
			<p class="about-tagline">Software engineer, dualist editor enthusiast, and open-source contributor.</p>
		</header>

		<hr />

		<section class="about-section">
			<h2>Background & Origins</h2>
			<p>
				I am a software engineer with academic and practical roots at the
				<strong>Silesian University of Technology</strong> (Faculty of Automatic Control, Electronics and Computer Science - AEI). <br
				/> My engineering interests lie at the intersection of low-level operating systems, kernel internals, and sovereign computing tools.
			</p>
			<p>
				My main portfolio and showcase can be found at
				<a href="https://szymon-wilczek.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">szymon-wilczek.me</a>, while this website serves as my
				independent hypermedia space for tools, personal archives, and technical explorations.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="about-section">
			<h2>The Dualist Philosophy (Neovim + Emacs)</h2>
			<p>
				Well, maybe some people would hang me for it, but in the long-standing text editor discourse, I belong firmly to the camp of the
				<strong>Dualists</strong>:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Neovim</strong>
					is my primary code-writing weapon and high-speed editing environment. I rely on it for the majority of my daily programming,
					build custom Lua plugins, and actively contribute to
					<a href="https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues?q=involves:szymonwilczek" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						Neovim upstream
					</a> to help make the editor even faster and more extensible.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>GNU Emacs</strong> serves as my mission control and operational headquarters. Powered by Org-mode, it drives my digital
					garden, agenda, and literate programming workflows, along with occasional Lisp hacking.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Rather than treating these tools as mutually exclusive (which most people do), I use the raw modal editing speed of Neovim
				alongside the limitless extensibility of Emacs to create perfect balance in the force.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="about-section">
			<h2>Upstream Contributions & Free Software</h2>
			<p>
				I believe deeply (really deeply) in the ethos of Free and Open Source Software (FOSS). As a matter of principle, I contribute
				back to the projects and tools I use:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>
						<a href="https://lore.kernel.org/all/?q=swilczek.lx@gmail.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Linux Kernel</a>
					</strong>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>
						<a href="https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues?q=involves:szymonwilczek" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							Neovim
						</a>
					</strong>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Independent Open Source</strong> - I am author of many bespoke tools, and editor packages, including
					<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek/typus-fonts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fonts</a>,
					<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek?tab=repositories&q=nvim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Neovim plugins</a>,
					<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek?tab=repositories&q=emacs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Emacs utilities</a>,
					and
					<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">more</a> suites.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="about-section">
			<h2>Bespoke Projects & Repositories</h2>
			<p>
				All of my independent experiments, and configurations are hosted on my
				<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub profile</a>. <br />I&apos;m still very depenent
				on GitHub infrastructure, maybe one day I&apos;ll transition to something else.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-header {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.about-tagline {
		font-family: 'Typus Mono 95', 'Typus Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		color: var(--fg-dim);
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.about-section {
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
	}

	.about-section h2 {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
	}

	.about-section ul {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		padding-left: 2rem;
	}

	.about-section li {
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
</style>
